    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="0872" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1416: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d617-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-09T18:00:00-05:00">October 9, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>69. Following strictly confidential telegram 70, October 9, noon, received from
                    Embassy Rio.</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of the telegram printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Department has replied today as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of telegram No. 70, October 9, 7 p.m., printed on <ref
                        target="#pg759">page 759</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Please take the matter up with Minister for Foreign Affairs in the sense of
                    instructions to the Ambassador at Rio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d617-f1" n="88" type="source" xml:id="d617-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date, to the
                    Ambassadors in Chile (No. 47) and Peru (No. 55).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
